{
 "version": 1,
 "about": "LEARNED by lookout_detect/learn.py (MAP Baum-Welch on emissions, Beta prior centred on the hand-set values). Lookout scam playbook model. One combined HMM: benign states (idle + look-alike activities) plus one branch of stages per scam playbook. Each observation is a SET of evidence flags seen together; each flag is an independent Bernoulli given the hidden state. Edit numbers here; Python (lookout_detect) and Swift (LookoutCore/Playbook) both read this file.",
 "events": [
  "URGENT_LANGUAGE",
  "PHONE_NUMBER_IN_POPUP",
  "BRAND_IMPERSONATION",
  "LOOKALIKE_DOMAIN",
  "INFECTED_CLAIM",
  "REFUND_OVERPAYMENT",
  "REMOTE_ACCESS_STARTED",
  "SCREEN_SHARE_ACTIVE",
  "BANK_SITE_OPENED",
  "SENSITIVE_FIELD_ON_UNKNOWN_SITE",
  "PAYMENT_DEMAND",
  "GIFT_CARD_PAGE",
  "WIRE_OR_CRYPTO_PAGE",
  "SECRECY_REQUEST",
  "FAMILY_EMERGENCY_STORY",
  "LEGAL_THREAT",
  "GOV_IMPERSONATION",
  "CLAUDE_FLAG"
 ],
 "model_reported_events": [
  "CLAUDE_FLAG"
 ],
 "model_reported_note": "Model-reported flags only count (present OR absent) on observations where the model actually ran. P(CLAUDE_FLAG | scam stage) ~0.9 and P(CLAUDE_FLAG | benign) = 0.045 come from the bench: Claude confirmation had 100% precision on 154 fixtures and ~90% recall when consulted; 0.045 (not ~0) caps one model report at log(0.9/0.045) = +3.0 nats so the model can never decide alone.",
 "distraction": 0.3,
 "distraction_why": "During any activity (a scam in progress, a family remote session) some screens are simply not about it: the person checks the weather, or the extractor misses a cue. Each non-idle state emits like idle with this probability: b_s(x) = (1 - d) * b_stage(x) + d * b_idle(x). Without it, one quiet screen collapses a real scam.",
 "probability_floor": 0.0001,
 "default_benign_rate": 0.002,
 "default_scam_rate": 0.01,
 "timing": {
  "scam_return_tau_s": 1800,
  "benign_return_tau_s": 900,
  "why": "Time between observations matters: a scam stage drifts back to idle with probability 1 - exp(-dt / tau). 30 min for scams (a remote-access launch 40 s after a fake pop-up is linked; three days later it is not), 15 min for benign activities."
 },
 "order": {
  "why": "State order shared by the Python and Swift engines (JSON object key order is not portable).",
  "benign": [
